      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, attempting to self-treat these potentially life-threatening symptoms with magnesium or hydration is extremely dangerous and could delay critical treatment for a stroke or TIA. Even if the weakness feels like a \"numbness\" rather than full paralysis, the combination of unilateral weakness and vision changes requires immediate medical imaging to rule out a serious neurological event. Please stop waiting and go to the emergency room right away, regardless of how you feel or what your friend suggests.",
